A||||12||Homicidal||Why are Fiero's looked down upon so MUCH?||||5||
Z||000000||Homicidal||04-15-2000||03:33 AM||||They are really good cars!  I know 1 in 23 can catch fire, but only in a certain year and model.  They may be plastic, but if you are a good driver you need not worry!<P>I think anybody who looks down upon this car must drive it first!  They are so fun and sporty!  I haven't met one Fiero owner who was unhappy yet!  <P>I beleive they *might* retain some sort of collectibility over the years.  The GTO was looked down upon a lot, and now they got for $50,000.  I beleive even the "Mustang" was thought of as a "crap" car.  <P>I just think people shouldn't put these beautiful cars down!  They have their flaws like every other car does, but they sure treat their owners well if they owners do the same!  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||stimpy||04-15-2000||08:39 AM||||I look down on my Fiero cuz it's only 43" high.||||reg||1
Z||000002||TheFiero64||04-15-2000||09:28 AM||||LOL, Stimpy. Homicidal, The fiero is & was one of the safest cars of all time. Its steel spaceframe is very rigid. It can be driven without the body panels and still hold its crash integrity. There are some web sites out there that explain the Fiero's safety level. I hope there are some forum members that can list the urls of those sites for us so you can read for yourself. I think that the reason people look down upon them is because they don't know the facts about them. They hear one story and stipulate about everything. I have turned a number of people around about the Fiero. You can too! Just hit them with the facts. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>P.S. I still do think of the Mustang as a crap car. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  (Just a joke no flame wars please  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )<BR><p>[This message has been edited by TheFiero64 (edited 04-15-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000003||Phaeton||04-15-2000||02:48 PM||||"I know my car better than you and I like it."  If they keep on talking I agree with them and even elaborate on the sortcomings, grinning and smiling the whole time.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||04-15-2000||03:24 PM||||Maybe because even many dwarves are taller than Fiero.<P>Mainly because the general public is retarded. They all hate Pinto too. I could haul more stuff with my Pinto than allot of cars twice as big. Had nearly 200,000 miles on it when I finally was forced by New Castle County to scrap it.<P>According to an advert I heard...... 1 in 10 of all cars catches fire. I find that easy to believe. The main reason is lack of proper service. followed closely by road debrise not promptly removed. ((Any time you run over anything make sure it came out the back. If it didn't find out why fast. No matter what kind of car it is.))||||reg||1
Z||000005||William||04-15-2000||04:31 PM||||Why do people think the fiero sucks?<P>#1 Money and GM mangement.<BR>Our poor fiero was touted as a sporty commuter rather than a sport car. Why, Because the Management wanted a bigger market for the fiero and did not want it labeled as just a two seater sports car which tend to have lowers sales. They also forced the engineers to redesign the suspension to use off the shelf componets. and lower the cost. When the expected problems for a newly designed car appeared, GM chose to ignore them rather than recall the cars and fix the problems. So, as the fires continued and the bad press began, (with GM not fixing the problems), the bad rumors and opinions began. GM killed their own baby.<P>#2 Car magazines<BR>Even though the reveiwers generally liked the Fiero, they threw stones at the handling. It seems that because the fiero looked like a Ferrari, they thought it must perform like one to. They did not seem to care that the car only cost 10 grand and a ferrari cost 50 grand. When the fires and other defects showed up, all the reviewers took back all the nice stuff they said in 84 and declared they fiero junk.<P>#3 Boring American consumers<BR>Even tho WE disagree the general pubic seems to be rather conserative and just doesn't like low mid engined cars with only two seats. Our neighbors seem to wrongly believe that engines should be in the front only, they feel ripped off if the car is missing the two rear seats, and very low cars just don't look like the buick that daddy used to drive. If you asked people on the street if they rather be given a Lotus espirt or a new Trans Am, the lotus will lose. Very sad indeed.<P>Why do I own one?<BR>I love mid engined two seaters. I can buy a well running Fiero for 1500. I can then restore it for no more than I could an escort. Other than a MR2, my only other choice is either a used Ferrari 308 or Espirt which will run you about 30 grand before you restore it....enough said<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000006||phillip||04-15-2000||04:42 PM||||shhhh...if no one wants them it makes them cheaper for me to buy.<P>i think along with the "facts" everyone hears about fieros is power out put. we all know it's an ever ongoing topic here. if the engine up grade was a little easier and/or less expensive, or of they would have gotten better engines to start with, they'd be much more popular. i know the import boys (can't really call them ricers. besides the fact that it sounds slightly racist,the majority of hot imports around here are vw's) look at my car as i try body mods and if i get a chance to change engines i think i'll change some minds.||||reg||1
Z||000007||frontal lobe||04-15-2000||11:35 PM||||If there ever was a prime example of the importance of first impressions, the fiero is it.  Nothing like a few hundred cars going up in flames to turn off the public.  Also, the fiero was a tease.  Beautiful looking body that you therefore expected to go faster than the 4-banger did.  Should have led with the 6.<P>The no back seat thing is interesting, because how inhabitable are most sporty car's back seats?  Yet a lot of people can't get past that.  <P>Oh well, at least that keeps the demand down some.||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||04-16-2000||10:45 PM||||How usefull are most rear seats at all. Have you actually tried to sit in a Saturn or Cavalier rear seat? Or a Tarus or most other cars in that size class? I haven't been able to get a good look yet, I hear Chrysler even hosed the Intrepid by making the rear seat unusable by an adult. (Gen 1 Intrepid was huge inside.)||||reg||1
Z||000009||DaRkLoRD||04-17-2000||12:26 AM||||I currently drive a 95 ford taurus, and Ogre is right. the back seat has no room.. unless you move the front seats all the way forward, in which case there's lots of room in the back. That's what I had to do the last time I cleaned it out.. speaking of which, I'll probably do the same thing later this week.. weather's finally nice.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Ozzy||04-17-2000||01:11 AM||||Allow me to shed my 'infinite' wisdom on this subject... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I read in a previous thread not too long ago something like this; Nearly everyone who puts the Fiero down has NEVER driven one!! I drive my 'little treasures' to my office frequently and just about everyone who works for me gave me a bunch of crap! <B>SO I FIRED 'EM!!</B>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  (just kidding) <P>Now nearly every one is on "Fiero Watch" in their daily travels and come back to the shop reporting to me "saw this nice maroon GT" and Theres another Fiero for sale! I got the number for you!<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000011||Haze_Performance||04-17-2000||04:24 AM||||Ok now that we are on the subject of PINHEADS!!!  talking junk about Fiero’s, This weekend I was at my local weekend street races. I drove my 92 Mustang GT droptop on Friday and as I drove down the strip I hear all the Camaro driving GM lovers talk much crap about Fords….. Fine I can take that (all I do then is fire the tires all the way down the strip and they all shut up)….But Saturday I drove my 85 2M4 and as I drove down the strip a idiot in a 93 Cavalier with a huge coffee can exhaust tip and 19” wheels said “look at the Pontiac Fairy “ AHHHHHH I couldn’t take it anymore I jumped out of the car and told the fool to pull his raggedy  ass car up to the line…he did and I was told I got him by 3 1/2  cars…..After the race I turned around and parked in his spot and all his friends came around and said how cool Fiero’s were……by the way he never came back….Wait until June when the V8 goes in, ill have a surprise for those Camaro guys…………. So I just want you all to know that I am standing up for Fiero rights… ||||reg||8
Z||000012||mshill||04-17-2000||11:46 AM||||It appears the ignorance may have an age limit (lower bounds) since yesterday I was just cruising over to the un-service station to put some air in the tires and went past two groups of high schoolers and got various comments like "those cars rock!" and "that is one of the coolest cars I have ever seen".<P>Of course, my white 86SE has a little better exhaust tone than stock with a +1 cam, ported exhaust and no cat. I also have some nice 5 spoke aluminum rims with 225/50R15 on the back and 205/50R15 on the front.||||reg||10
